{"id":"[REDACTED]","object":"chat.completion","created":1788222349,"model":"mercury-2","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"**Concrete break:** The repository contains hard‑coded credential values that are detected as non‑placeholder secrets by the secret‑scanner test suite. This makes the current codebase insecure and causes the `dashboard-token-leak-static.test.js` suite to fail.\n\n**Evidence**\n\n* `test/mercury-llm-config-contract.test.js` contains a literal API‑key string:\n\n  ```js\n  100 |        provider: 'openai', model: 'kimi‑k3', apiKey: '[REDACTED]', authRequired: true,\n  ```\n\n  (line 100 of `test/mercury-llm-config-contract.test.js` – see the opened file excerpt.)\n\n* The secret‑scanner test reports many non‑placeholder findings, e.g.:\n\n  ```\n  FAIL test/dashboard-token-leak-static.test.js (30.497 s)\n    ● dashboard websocket token containment › tracked files do not contain dashboard token secrets\n\n      Command failed: node scripts/scan-secrets.js --tracked\n      [secret-scan] Found 15 secret finding(s):\n      - ogz-meta/inbox/amp/2026-08-29/record-the-rulings/EVIDENCE.md:300 JSON credential apiKeySource contains a non‑placeholder value\n      - ogz-meta/inbox/amp/2026-08-29/record-the-rulings/EVIDENCE.md:494 JSON credential apiKeySource contains a non‑placeholder value\n      …\n      - test/mercury-llm-config-contract.test.js:100 object credential apiKey contains a non‑placeholder value\n      - test/mercury-llm-config-contract.test.js:102 object credential MOONSHOT_API_KEY contains a non‑placeholder value\n  ```\n\n  (excerpt from the full test‑run output – see the `dashboard-token‑leak‑static.test.js` failure block.)\n\nThese findings demonstrate that the current codebase leaks real secret values, which is a concrete failure of the fix (the system should never contain such literals). The presence of these hard‑coded secrets breaks the security guarantees expected from the platform.","tool_calls":[],"tool_call